WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.135
- Hello, I'm Gav.
- I'm Dan.

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.369 align:start position:0%
We're The Slow Mo Guys,

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:05.071 align:start position:0%
 and this week on 
"The Super Slow Show,"

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:06.272 size:75% position:38%
what have we got, Dan?

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:07.573 align:end position:100%
This week's
all about vehicles.

00:00:07.606 --> 00:00:08.775 align:end position:100%
You could say we're
in the slow lane.

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.176
- Excellent pun.
- Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:12.211 align:start position:0%
Excellent name
for the week, I think.

00:00:12.244 --> 00:00:13.579 align:start position:0%
Although our vehicles
aren't really gonna be

00:00:13.612 --> 00:00:15.114 align:start position:0%
in a particular lane,
I would say.

00:00:15.147 --> 00:00:16.749 align:end position:100%
More like to be like
in a crumpled heap, I think.

00:00:16.782 --> 00:00:19.585
Yeah. But crumpled heaps look
much better in slow motion.

00:00:19.618 --> 00:00:21.654
Dan: <i> We're going to be shaving
 the top off a moving truck</i>

00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:24.290
<i>and crashing two cars together
 as fast as we can.</i>

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:26.059
- I'm excited.
- Me, too.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.427
<i> ( theme music playing )</i>

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:37.170 align:start position:0%
One of the most requested
subjects

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.305 align:start position:0%
for a slow mo ever since we
started this channel

00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:40.640 align:start size:97% position:3%
was a car crash.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.308 align:start position:0%
And because we don't like
letting you down,

00:00:42.341 --> 00:00:43.810 size:75% position:38%
we've finally done it,

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.178 align:start position:0%
and it only took us
seven years.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.479 align:start size:72% position:28%
Yeah, only seven years.

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:48.414 align:end position:100%
Mainly because I didn't want
to trash my car,

00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:50.083 align:end position:100%
and there's not enough room
in your back garden,

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.084 align:start size:78% position:22%
and also you don't drive.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.418 align:start size:97% position:3%
This is correct.

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:53.786 align:start position:0%
So we had a word with
our special effects team.

00:00:53.819 --> 00:00:55.154 align:start position:0%
They said we can get 

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:57.390 align:start position:0%
a 25-mile-an-hour speed
on each car

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:59.192
for a 50-mile-an-hour impact.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.326
Yeah, we were like,
"No, no, no,

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:01.527
We don't want a fender bender.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.463 align:end position:100%
We want to annihilate
the cars.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:04.564 align:start size:56% position:44%
Can we double it?"

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.532 align:start position:0%
And they said,
"Now we're talking."

00:01:06.565 --> 00:01:08.768 size:88% position:44%
So now we're about to film

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:11.737 align:start position:0%
a 100-mile-an-hour
head-on impact

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:13.506
at a thousand frames a second.

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:14.841 align:start position:0%
And we've even got
the tight angle

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.275 align:start position:0%
running at 2,000.

00:01:16.308 --> 00:01:17.710
- Isn't that nice?
- Cheeky.

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:18.744 size:81% position:41%
Let's look at our setup.

00:01:18.777 --> 00:01:20.313 align:start size:72% position:28%
People may be wondering

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:21.747 align:end position:100%
how we're gonna manage
to crash two cars

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.783 align:end position:100%
into each other without
anyone driving them.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:26.819 align:end position:100%
The method we've got
is we've got a tow car here,
or a truck--

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:28.621
- Beastly.
- Beastly.

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:31.190
And you've got two cables
coming from it here and here.

00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:33.860
They go from
the end of the truck

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.328
through this pulley

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.163
to one of our cars,

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:39.365
and then through this pulley
to the other car,

00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:41.501
so they're going to come in
at the same direction.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.469
So as this car drives off
into the distance,

00:01:43.502 --> 00:01:45.338
the cars just get pulled
straight into each other.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.672 align:start position:0%
So this truck
will drive off.

00:01:46.705 --> 00:01:48.141 align:start position:0%
When it hits
50 miles an hour,

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.476 align:start position:0%
the cars will be
about 14 feet apart,

00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:52.478
at which point

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:53.813
this metal cable

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:55.481
will turn to be taut

00:01:55.514 --> 00:01:58.251
and it's gonna unlock this

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.785 align:end position:100%
so that it doesn't rip
the back of the truck out.

00:01:59.818 --> 00:02:01.220 align:start position:0%
Quite a feat of engineering,
all this.

00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:02.221
It really is.

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:03.422
It's quite elaborate.

00:02:03.455 --> 00:02:05.725
But it's gonna work,
essentially,

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.260
'cause we need to guarantee

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:08.494
that they're gonna hit
in the right spot

00:02:08.527 --> 00:02:10.229
so we can get it
on the Phantoms.

00:02:10.262 --> 00:02:12.165
That's true
'cause one of our angles
is pretty tight.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.533
- Yeah.
- Pretty tight.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.568 align:start position:0%
Okay, so you're responsible
for this car.

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:18.504
Yeah, I came up with a little
bit of character design

00:02:18.537 --> 00:02:20.206 align:end position:100%
for the guy
who would drive this car.

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:21.874
- Okay.
- He was a clown, actually.

00:02:21.907 --> 00:02:23.409 align:start position:0%
Do you mean like literally
or just an idiot?

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:25.511 align:end position:100%
No, an actual clown,
a working clown.

00:02:25.544 --> 00:02:28.948 align:end position:100%
He would frequently transport
balloons full of paint,
as they do.

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:30.650 size:84% position:58%
Clowns are famous for that.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.618 size:84% position:58%
I'm going to put this one
on the shelf back here.

00:02:32.651 --> 00:02:34.554 align:end position:100%
All right.
So that one should go.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.722 align:start position:0%
So when it crashes,
it gets some height,

00:02:36.755 --> 00:02:38.357 align:start position:0%
and it maybe will come
through the glass.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:40.359
- Yeah, that'll be nice.
- I like it. Yeah.

00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:43.863
- So here's your car.
- Yep.

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:46.699 align:start position:0%
What was your person
doing for a living?

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:48.968
Well, mine was actually
a fruit salesman,

00:02:49.001 --> 00:02:50.703
but he'd fallen
upon hard times.

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:52.572
So he couldn't have
a cart anymore.

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.273
So he had to just put
all his fruit in the car.

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:56.609 align:start position:0%
So it's like a 2008-era
fruit man.

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:58.444
So these are slightly
heftier than paint

00:02:58.477 --> 00:03:00.279
- 'cause they're slightly
 harder.
- Yeah.

00:03:00.312 --> 00:03:02.381
So I'm expecting maybe some
to go through the windscreen,

00:03:02.414 --> 00:03:03.549
or something like that.

00:03:03.582 --> 00:03:04.917
I'm just gonna lob them in.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.620
Here, just straddle
the GoPro with melons.

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:09.655 align:end position:100%
So we're up here.
We've been harnessed in.

00:03:09.688 --> 00:03:13.226 align:end position:100%
So-- I mean, if any car parts
come flying towards us,

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.760 align:end position:100%
there's no chance
that we can get
out of the way.

00:03:14.793 --> 00:03:16.796 size:84% position:42%
Just have to duck, I guess.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.664 align:end position:100%
Yeah, but at least
we won't fall three feet
to the containers.

00:03:18.697 --> 00:03:19.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's true.

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:20.967
Also we're up here
with the cameraman,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.501 size:84% position:58%
who's the only other person

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:23.869 align:end position:100%
that actually has
a good vantage point,

00:03:23.902 --> 00:03:24.971 align:start size:72% position:28%
but he can't look at it

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.505 align:end position:100%
because he's
looking at us.

00:03:26.538 --> 00:03:28.307 align:start position:0%
So we're going to take
a bullet for Tony

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.875 align:start position:0%
if a tire hub
comes our way.

00:03:29.908 --> 00:03:32.311 align:end position:100%
So if a wheel comes flying
at him,

00:03:32.344 --> 00:03:34.247
- I guess... that's it.
- Okay.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.281
Are you ready?

00:03:35.314 --> 00:03:36.549 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think we're ready.

00:03:36.582 --> 00:03:37.783
- Yeah?
- I'm nervous but I'm ready.

00:03:37.816 --> 00:03:42.989
Okay.
Right, three, two, one, go!

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.590 align:start size:97% position:3%
Off he goes.

00:03:44.623 --> 00:03:48.828 align:start position:0%
- Oh, no, the concrete's moving.
- Is that an issue?

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:49.862
I think so.

00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:53.866
It's an issue.

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:57.003
- Oh!
- Dan: Oh, man!

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.804
Oh.

00:03:58.837 --> 00:04:02.441
That didn't work.
( bleep )

00:04:02.474 --> 00:04:05.378
Dan: The concrete moved.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.747
- Oh, man.
- So...

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.615
the sort of anchorage point

00:04:09.648 --> 00:04:11.951
on the concrete--

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:13.686
the concrete
wasn't heavy enough.

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:15.054
- So I imagine--
- Dragged it.

00:04:15.087 --> 00:04:17.757 align:start position:0%
It dragged it, like,
15 feet almost.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.493
Dan: <i> Because it missed
 our Phantoms.</i>

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:22.595
Gav: <i> I think we have
 to do it again.</i>

00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:23.929
Dan: <i> Yeah.</i>

00:04:23.962 --> 00:04:25.765 align:start position:0%
Thankfully it'll be
really cheap

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:27.467 align:start position:0%
and not a big deal
in any way.

00:04:30.602 --> 00:04:33.005
And just like that,
some time has passed.

00:04:33.038 --> 00:04:35.775
We have two brand new cars
fully loaded

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:37.443
<i> with the same exact items.</i>

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:38.778 align:end position:100%
Yeah, last time we had
a bit of a failure

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:40.713 align:start size:78% position:22%
because we had one K-rail

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:42.648
which was used as the anchor
point with the pulleys on,

00:04:42.681 --> 00:04:44.417 align:end position:100%
but the weight
of the K-rail

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.818 align:end position:100%
was too similar
to the two cars
being pulled,

00:04:45.851 --> 00:04:46.852 align:end position:100%
which meant
that the timing was off

00:04:46.885 --> 00:04:48.387 align:end position:100%
'cause they
got yanked away,

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:49.955 align:end position:100%
so this time,
we've doubled the K-rails

00:04:49.988 --> 00:04:51.957 align:end position:100%
and we've also put three-foot
pins into the ground.

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:53.793 align:end position:100%
So hopefully this time there
well be no mess ups

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:55.761 align:end position:100%
and we'll get that exact
perfect smush that we want.

00:04:55.794 --> 00:04:57.496
And the drag of the K-rails

00:04:57.529 --> 00:04:59.031
just slowed down the rate
that they hit each other,

00:04:59.064 --> 00:05:00.833
so now they should hit
a lot harder,

00:05:00.866 --> 00:05:02.802
right in the middle
where we want them.

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.470
Good luck, us.

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:05.504 align:start size:69% position:31%
You nervous this time?

00:05:05.537 --> 00:05:06.939
Well, second time's the charm.

00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:10.343 align:start position:0%
And I say that because
we can't afford to do it again.

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:12.511 size:88% position:44%
So let's see what happens.

00:05:12.544 --> 00:05:15.614 align:end position:100%
Maybe we'd be even
more tanned and injured
the next time we try it.

00:05:15.647 --> 00:05:16.816
Right?

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:18.617 align:start position:0%
- All right, I think I'm ready.
- Okay.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:21.854
Three, two, one, go!

00:05:21.887 --> 00:05:23.356
Gav: Keep an eye
on the K-rail.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:24.857
- Dan: This is great.
- Gav: Come on.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:26.359
Dan: He's bookin'.
He's bookin'.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:29.528
Come on. Come on.

00:05:29.561 --> 00:05:30.996
( together )
Ooh!

00:05:31.029 --> 00:05:32.064
Dan: What?

00:05:32.097 --> 00:05:33.466
( together )
Ooh!

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:36.502 align:start position:0%
Oh, my God.
Oh!

00:05:36.535 --> 00:05:38.871 align:start position:0%
Dan: Look at the steam
escaping from there!

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:40.573
That was class.

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:42.508
It was like the front
of the cars burst.

00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:43.843
Did you see that?

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:45.745 align:start position:0%
Gav: There was a lot of debris
in the air there.

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.380 align:start position:0%
- There was.
- I can't wait to see that back.

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:48.781 align:end position:100%
That went, like, 20 feet.
That was amazing.

00:05:50.449 --> 00:05:54.387 size:78% position:39%
 Gav: <i> That went not bad.
That is almost dead on.</i>

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.889
Dan: <i> Oh, the wheel moves,
 on the left-hand side one.</i>

00:05:56.922 --> 00:05:59.525 align:start size:72% position:28%
<i> Look, the back wheels
 are off the floor.</i>

00:05:59.558 --> 00:06:02.428 align:start position:0%
<i>Oh, look at that melon
coming out.</i>

00:06:02.461 --> 00:06:03.863 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> So the back car...</i>

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:05.498 align:start size:56% position:44%
<i> Look at how high
 off the ground</i>

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:07.433 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> the back-- the right-hand
 side car is.</i>

00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:08.801 align:start size:66% position:34%
<i> It's just taken off.</i>

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:10.370 align:start position:0%
<i>That's great.</i>

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.145
<i> Whoa.</i>

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:20.579
<i> Look at the front wheel there.</i>

00:06:20.612 --> 00:06:22.148 align:start size:69% position:31%
<i> It just gets smushed.</i>

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:23.949 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> And then all these melons
 start flying.</i>

00:06:23.982 --> 00:06:27.486 align:start position:0%
<i>And the melons pushed loads
of shards of glass out.</i>

00:06:27.519 --> 00:06:29.588
<i> So it wasn't even the crash
 that smashed the glass.</i>

00:06:29.621 --> 00:06:31.624
<i> It was the melons hitting
 the glass that smashed it.</i>

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:33.459 align:start position:0%
<i>You would not wanna be
in there.</i>

00:06:33.492 --> 00:06:35.128
- <i> No, you wouldn't. </i>
- <i> And I'm glad no one was.</i>

00:06:54.012 --> 00:06:55.815
Think you got a flat
on the front of that one.

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:57.450
That is exactly
what we wanted. Look.

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:59.752 align:start position:0% line:0%
That's the GoPro
that was in the middle
of the--

00:06:59.785 --> 00:07:02.188
Oh, it's not even destroyed!
Perfect.

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:03.889
- Gav: Listen to the hiss.
- Dan: What's that noise?
 What is that?

00:07:03.922 --> 00:07:05.624
I think it's the Freon
leaking out.

00:07:05.657 --> 00:07:06.992
I think it's the air
conditioning.

00:07:07.025 --> 00:07:08.494 align:end position:100%
Maybe you should sit
on that car.

00:07:08.527 --> 00:07:11.530 align:end position:100%
Then there'd be
"free" on that car, too.

00:07:11.563 --> 00:07:12.765
- ( chuckles )
- I'm sorry.

00:07:12.798 --> 00:07:14.767 align:end position:100%
It looks like it's bleeding.
You see that?

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:17.136 align:start position:0%
That's, like, pretty hectic.
Isn't it?

00:07:17.169 --> 00:07:18.537 align:start position:0%
All right, let's take
a look inside, shall we?

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:20.206 align:start size:47% position:53%
Yeah, for sure.

00:07:20.239 --> 00:07:23.509 align:start position:0%
Gav: That's actually given
a quite nice, colorful
paint job here.

00:07:23.542 --> 00:07:26.679 align:start position:0%
That is an absolute
fruit massacre.

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:27.847 size:84% position:58%
Smells really good, though.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.014 align:start position:0%
It smells tremendous.

00:07:29.047 --> 00:07:30.249 size:88% position:56%
It's like the mix of sort of

00:07:30.282 --> 00:07:33.719 align:end position:100%
early '90s car smell
and watermelon.

00:07:33.752 --> 00:07:37.490 align:start position:0%
The amount that's just wedged up
against the windscreen
and the dashboard.

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:40.693 align:start position:0%
It's all smushed
to the front.

00:07:40.726 --> 00:07:42.228 size:78% position:39%
I think that looked about
as beautiful as it could

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:44.063 size:78% position:39%
for what the subject was.

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:45.598 align:end position:100%
That's something
I've always wanted to do.

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:47.066 align:end position:100%
What always amazes me
is the fact that--

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:49.268 align:end position:100%
of how much power
is involved and how much force

00:07:49.301 --> 00:07:52.104 align:end position:100%
because can you imagine
just trying to push this
with your hand? 

00:07:52.137 --> 00:07:54.707 align:end position:100%
You can't do anything,
but when there's two cars
hitting each other,

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.242 align:end position:100%
it's like paper
just being ripped apart.

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:58.277 size:78% position:39%
At high speed it's almost
like tin foil crumpling,

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:01.881 align:start position:0%
and then you realize
it's bloody solid metal.

00:08:01.914 --> 00:08:03.949
- Yeah.
- Hopefully you enjoyed
  that car crash.

00:08:03.982 --> 00:08:05.718 align:start position:0%
Feel free to subscribe
to the Slow Mo Guys,

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:07.019 align:start position:0%
and we'll see you
in the next episode

